I believe I have found a (minor) bug, but am asking all you Nethackers
to help verify my "facts" before I send it to the dev team.  If this
is a known bug, I'd appreciate feedback so as not to pursue it
further. 

=====

The pick-axe is a two-handed weapon.  (Is this right?)

If you try to wield it while wearing a shield, the program won't let
you.  (Is this right?)

However, you can apply it while wearing a shield.  (Is this right?)

After digging with it, you are now wielding it.  If you now hit a
monster, you'll get a "bashing" message.  (I know these are right.)

But as far as I can tell (from the code) you do not incur any penalty
for now wielding a two-handed weapon while wearing a shield.  (Is this
right?)

=====

Admittedly, this is not a big bug, as people would usually switch to a
more powerful weapon since a pick-axe only does 1-6 points of damage
against small monsters and 1-3 against large ones. 



